#: src/algebra/redundant.md:119
msgid "\"Reverse the withdrawal directions\""
msgstr "\"Reverse the withdrawal directions\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:120
msgid "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, before bar\""
msgstr "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, before bar\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:121
msgid "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, after bar\""
msgstr "\"Withdrawal plus its hat, after bar\""

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:141
msgid ""
"`Yen cash postings before aggregation` retains the separate withdrawal and "
"payment amounts. `Cash balances by currency` contains the net cash changes "
"in yen and dollars, while `Yen posting total` counts the gross yen amounts "
"on every account. `Yen cash totals by direction` contains the separate "
"increase and decrease totals. The named withdrawal-plus-hat results "
"distinguish retaining opposing postings from canceling them with bar."
msgstr ""
"`Yen cash postings before aggregation` は, 引き出しと支払いの金額を別々に保持"
"しています. `Cash balances by currency` は円とドルの現金の純変化を含み, `Yen "
"posting total` はすべての勘定科目にわたる円金額の総額を数えます. `Yen cash "
"totals by direction` は増加と減少の合計を別々に含みます. 引き出しとその hat "
"の和の名前付きの結果では, 逆方向の項を保持する場合と, bar で相殺する場合を区"
"別しています."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:143
msgid ""
"The displayed sequence order can differ from the source expression's order. "
"Construction routes can arrange the same postings differently, and "
"structural `Eq` can observe that arrangement. Do not infer chronological "
"order from the printed algebra. When comparing aggregated content, choose an "
"explicit `compress` or `bar` according to whether the opposing directions "
"must remain separate."
msgstr ""
"表示される列の順序は, 元の式の順序と異なる場合があります. 構築経路によって同"
"じ項の並び方が変わり, 構造的な `Eq` はその並び方を区別できます. 表示された代"
"数から時系列の順序を推測しないでください. 集約した内容を比較するときは, 逆方"
"向を別々に保持する必要があるかに応じて, `compress` または `bar` を明示的に選"
"んでください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:149
msgid "Construction and operations"
msgstr "構築と演算"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:151
msgid ""
"`Alg` requires a `HatVal` amount type and a `HatBaseClass` base type. Its "
"`Redundant` instance implements the operations; defining a new coordinate "
"type does not require another `Redundant` instance. `Zero` is the empty "
"algebra and the identity for addition. For value and direction checks, see "
"[Construction and scalar checks](values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)."
msgstr ""
"`Alg` は金額の型に `HatVal` を, 基底の型に `HatBaseClass` を要求します. その "
"`Redundant` の instance が演算を実装します. 新しい座標の型を定義しても, 別の "
"`Redundant` の instance は不要です. `Zero` は空の代数であり, 加算の単位元で"
"す. 値と方向の検査については, [構築時とスカラーの検査]"
"(values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:153
msgid ""
"The public `(:@)` pattern matches a singleton posting but cannot construct "
"one in 0.6.0.1. Construct postings with `.@`. `toList` returns singleton "
"postings, `vals` returns amounts, and `bases` returns hat bases."
msgstr ""
"公開パターン `(:@)` は単一の項に一致しますが, 0.6.0.1 では項を構築できませ"
"ん. 項は `.@` で構築してください. `toList` は単一の項を並べたリストを, "
"`vals` は金額を, `bases` は hat 基底を返します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:155 src/exchange/exchange.md:104
#: src/exchange/transfer.md:121 src/journal/journal.md:180
#: src/journal/agents.md:138
msgid "Inputs and result"
msgstr "入力と結果"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:157
msgid "`x .+ y`"
msgstr "`x .+ y`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:157
msgid ""
"Retain the postings from both algebras. Equal bases do not cause immediate "
"summation or cancellation. `(<>)` is the same addition."
msgstr ""
"両方の代数の項を保持します. 基底が等しくても, 即座の合算や相殺は行いません. "
"`(<>)` も同じ加算です."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:158
msgid "`scalar .* x`"
msgstr "`scalar .* x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:158
msgid ""
"Multiply every amount by the scalar, preserving the posting structure except "
"for zero products. See the input checks in [Values](values.md#construction-"
"and-scalar-checks)."
msgstr ""
"各金額をスカラー倍し, 積がゼロになる場合を除いて項の構造を保持します. [値]"
"(values.md#construction-and-scalar-checks)の入力検査を参照してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:159
msgid "`norm x`"
msgstr "`norm x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:159
msgid ""
"Total all stored amounts on both directions. Return an amount, losing base "
"and direction information."
msgstr ""
"両方向に記録されたすべての金額を合計します. 金額を返し, 基底と方向の情報は失"
"われます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:160
msgid "`bar x`, also written `(.-) x`"
msgstr "`bar x` または `(.-) x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:160
msgid ""
"Total the opposing directions at each full base and keep only the excess on "
"the winning direction. Remove an exactly canceled base."
msgstr ""
"完全な基底ごとに逆方向の金額を合計し, 大きい方向の超過分だけを残します. 完全"
"に相殺された基底を取り除きます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:161
msgid "`compress x`"
msgstr "`compress x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:161
msgid ""
"Total each direction at each full base separately, without cancellation. "
"This explicitly discards the separate postings within each direction."
msgstr ""
"完全な基底ごとに各方向を別々に合計し, 相殺しません. 各方向の個々の項は明示的"
"に捨てます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:162
msgid "`(.^) x`"
msgstr "`(.^) x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:162
msgid "Swap `Hat` and `Not` for every posting, preserving each amount."
msgstr "各金額を保持し, すべての項の `Hat` と `Not` を入れ替えます."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:163
msgid "`proj patterns x`"
msgstr "`proj patterns x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:163
msgid ""
"Select postings whose hat bases match at least one query pattern, without "
"netting or changing amounts."
msgstr ""
"hat 基底が少なくとも 1 つの問い合わせパターンに一致する項を選択し, 相殺や金額"
"の変更は行いません."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:164
msgid "`projNetNorm patterns x`"
msgstr "`projNetNorm patterns x`"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:164
msgid ""
"Select bases, net within each full base, total the magnitudes of the "
"residuals, and round once. Return an amount."
msgstr ""
"基底を選択し, 完全な基底ごとに相殺し, 残差の大きさを合計して 1 回だけ丸めま"
"す. 金額を返します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:166
msgid ""
"In 0.6.0.1, `.*` has the default fixity `infixl 9`, and `.+` is `infixr 3`. "
"Parenthesize mixed expressions to state the intended grouping, such as "
"`(2 .* withdrawal) .+ cashPayment`."
msgstr ""
"0.6.0.1 では, `.*` の結合性と優先順位は既定の `infixl 9` で, `.+` は `infixr "
"3` です. 演算を混ぜた式は, `(2 .* withdrawal) .+ cashPayment` のように括弧で"
"意図したまとまりを示してください."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:168
msgid "Projections and rounding"
msgstr "射影と丸め"

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:170
msgid ""
"Overlapping or repeated `proj` patterns select each posting once. "
"`projByAccountTitle` from `ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange`, also re-"
"exported by `ExchangeAlgebra`, selects an account across the other axes."
msgstr ""
"`proj` のパターンが重複していても, 各項は 1 回だけ選択されます. "
"`ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange` の `projByAccountTitle` は, "
"`ExchangeAlgebra` からも再エクスポートされており, 他の軸にわたって勘定科目を"
"選択します."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:172
msgid ""
"`bar` and `projNetNorm` net within each full base; yen and dollar cash "
"cannot cancel each other. For exact decimal amounts, `projNetNorm patterns "
"x` agrees with `norm (bar (proj patterns x))`. Floating-point results can "
"differ because the latter expression rounds each base's residual before "
"summing."
msgstr ""
"`bar` と `projNetNorm` は完全な基底ごとに相殺するので, 円とドルの現金は互いに"
"相殺できません. 正確な十進数の金額では, `projNetNorm patterns x` は `norm "
"(bar (proj patterns x))` と一致します. 浮動小数点の結果は, 後者の式が合計の前"
"に各基底の残差を丸めるため, 異なる場合があります."

#: src/algebra/redundant.md:174
msgid ""
"**Caution:** `compress` discards separate posting amounts, and floating-"
"point rounding of the direction totals can change the result of a later "
"`bar`. Preserve the original algebra when individual postings are needed."
msgstr ""
"**注意:** `compress` は個々の項の金額を捨てます. また, 方向別の合計に対する浮"
"動小数点の丸めにより, その後の `bar` の結果が変わる場合があります. 個々の項が"
"必要な場合は, 元の代数を保持してください."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:3
msgid ""
"The January 10 withdrawal has a debit of 3,000 yen to Cash and a credit of "
"3,000 yen to Deposits. An exchange algebra is a redundant algebra with "
"account classifications on its bases and decompositions into debit and "
"credit postings. The classifications correspond to [Definition 7](../algebra/"
"definitions.md#account-classes-and-sides), and the decompositions correspond "
"to [Definition 8](../algebra/definitions.md#debit-and-credit-decomposition)."
msgstr ""
"1 月 10 日の引き出しでは, 借方に現金 3,000 円, 貸方に預金 3,000 円を記録しま"
"す. 交換代数は, 基底に勘定科目の区分を持ち, 項を借方と貸方に分解できる冗長代"
"数です. 区分は[定義 7](../algebra/definitions.md#account-classes-and-sides), "
"分解は[定義 8](../algebra/definitions.md#debit-and-credit-decomposition)に対"
"応します."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:5
msgid ""
"Use exchangealgebra-0.6.0.1 in the project prepared in [Add the package to a "
"Stack project](../usage/installation.md#add-the-package-to-a-stack-project). "
"The example keeps the custom `Unit` and the account-and-unit base from [The "
"redundant algebra](../algebra/redundant.md). It adds an instance for account "
"access, then checks the withdrawal's sides and balance."
msgstr ""
"[Stack プロジェクトにパッケージを追加する](../usage/installation.md#add-the-"
"package-to-a-stack-project)に従い, exchangealgebra-0.6.0.1 を使ってください. "
"例では[冗長代数](../algebra/redundant.md)で使った自作の `Unit` と勘定科目と単"
"位の基底を保ちます. 勘定科目へアクセスする instance を加えて, 引き出しの貸借"
"の側と均衡を確かめます."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:7
msgid "Declare the base instance"
msgstr "基底の instance を宣言する"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:9
msgid ""
"Save the code blocks in their displayed order as `Main.hs`. Declare how to "
"read and replace the account title in the custom base:"
msgstr ""
"コードブロックを表示順に `Main.hs` として保存してください. 自作の基底から勘定"
"科目を読み出し, 置き換える方法を宣言してください:"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:29 src/exchange/transfer.md:29
#: src/journal/journal.md:30
msgid "-- | Account access for the custom account-and-currency base.\n"
msgstr "-- | 自作の勘定科目と通貨の基底で勘定科目へアクセスします.\n"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:36
msgid ""
"`FlexibleInstances` is needed for the instance head `HatBase (AccountTitles, "
"Unit)`. `DeriveGeneric` and `DeriveAnyClass` supply the `Hashable` instance "
"for `Unit`. `ExchangeAlgebra` re-exports the types and classes used by these "
"declarations; the accounting classes are also available from "
"`ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange`."
msgstr ""
"`FlexibleInstances` は instance の頭部 `HatBase (AccountTitles, Unit)` に必要"
"です. `DeriveGeneric` と `DeriveAnyClass` は `Unit` に `Hashable` instance を"
"備えます. `ExchangeAlgebra` はこれらの宣言に使う型とクラスを再公開します. 会"
"計のクラスは `ExchangeAlgebra.Accounting.Exchange` からも利用できます."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:38
msgid ""
"The built-in `ExBaseClass` instances cover several specific base shapes, but "
"do not cover this custom account-and-unit base. Define `getAccountTitle` and "
"`setAccountTitle`. The setter retains direction and currency. The remaining "
"methods have defaults derived from the account title and direction, so no "
"new `Exchange` instance is needed for `Alg`."
msgstr ""
"組み込みの `ExBaseClass` instance は複数の具体的な基底の形に対応しますが, こ"
"の自作の勘定科目と単位の基底には対応しません. `getAccountTitle` と "
"`setAccountTitle` を定義してください. setter は方向と通貨を保持します. 残りの"
"メソッドには勘定科目と方向から導く既定の実装があるので, `Alg` に新たな "
"`Exchange` instance は不要です."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:40
msgid "Record the withdrawal"
msgstr "引き出しを記録する"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:42
msgid "Construct the two postings with positive amounts:"
msgstr "正の額で 2 つの項を構築してください:"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:51
msgid ""
"Cash and Deposits are assets. An asset increase is a debit, so `Not :< "
"(Cash, Yen)` is a debit. An asset decrease is a credit, so `Hat :< "
"(Deposits, Yen)` is a credit. The home side is the side for an increase: "
"debit for an ordinary asset or expense, credit for an ordinary liability, "
"equity account, or revenue. Contra accounts reverse their division's home "
"side."
msgstr ""
"現金と預金は資産です. 資産の増加は借方なので, `Not :< (Cash, Yen)` は借方で"
"す. 資産の減少は貸方なので, `Hat :< (Deposits, Yen)` は貸方です. 本来の貸借の"
"側とは増加を記録する側です. 通常の資産と費用は借方, 通常の負債, 資本, 収益は"
"貸方になります. 評価勘定は属する区分の本来の貸借の側を逆にします."

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:53
msgid "Decompose and check the record"
msgstr "記録を分解して確かめる"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:55
msgid ""
"Select the two sides with `decL` and `decR`, total each side with `norm`, "
"and check exact equality with `balance`:"
msgstr ""
"`decL` と `decR` で貸借の側を選び, `norm` で各側を合計し, `balance` で厳密な"
"一致を確かめてください:"

#: src/exchange/exchange.md:61
msgid ""
